  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_scope",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1740,
        "y": 0
      },
      "text": "REAR WHEEL SPEED - two pieces. IN: the RL and RR ABS drops run as separate cables to a point by the IN plug and land in it. OUT: the OUT plug, the screened 4-core output cable and the 6-way inline DT04-6P near the ECU (IX_WS_REAR). The ECU side owns only the short spur and the DT06-6S mating half. No bulkhead."
    },
    {
      "id": "n_vrc",
      "width": 390,
      "color": "Orange",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1740,
        "y": 210
      },
      "text": "VRC NOT DRAWN. The VR conditioner and its enclosure belong to the enclosure build. This harness is two separate pieces with no drawn link (Daniel 2026-10-12): IN - the RL and RR legs land in the IN plug lp16_vrc_r_in (pin 1 ABS+ RL, 2 ABS- RL, 3 shield drain, 4 ABS+ RR, 5 ABS- RR); OUT - the OUT plug lp16_vrc_r_out (pin 1 +5V, 2 Gnd, 3 RL out, 4 RR out, 5 screen drain) -> 4-core screened cable -> IX_WS_REAR c1-c5 (c6 spare). Both plugs: CNLINKO LP-16-J05PE-02-001, female, 5 pins, unshielded, solder cups 22-20 AWG; the box takes the LP-16-C05SX-02-101 rear-nut panel socket."
    },
    {
      "id": "n_shield",
      "width": 390,
      "color": "Orange",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1740,
        "y": 480
      },
      "text": "SHIELDS (docs/SHIELD-RULES.md; no connector shells, drains on pins). Each sensor screen floats at the sensor. Every screen is drawn as if it had a drain wire (R29): both sensor screens meet at ONE splice by the IN plug and one drain wire (M22759/16-20-06) runs from it to IN pin 3. Build method, not drawn (R30): the RL drain is the one crimped (soldered) into IN pin 3; the RR drain is soldered onto it about 6 mm (0.25 in) behind the rear of the plug, where 6 mm of the RL drain's insulation is cut away. The output cable screen lands straight on OUT pin 5 and on inline pin 5, which runs on to the ECU shield ground. Inside the VRC the build joins IN pin 3 to OUT pin 5 by wire. One screen node, grounded once, at the ECU."
    },
    {
      "id": "n_iso",
      "width": 390,
      "color": "Red",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1740,
        "y": 870
      },
      "text": "ISOLATION. The PCB must not touch the enclosure - nylon standoffs; the board grounds through the output cable only. The screen never touches the case either: the drains run pin to pin inside the box. Mount the enclosure on nylon hardware."
    },
    {
      "id": "n_coat",
      "width": 390,
      "color": "Red",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1740,
        "y": 1080
      },
      "text": "NO CONNECTOR OR CASE LANDINGS FOR THE SCREEN. Drains run by pin (IN 3, OUT 5) and join inside the box by wire - nothing bonds to the case and no connector shell carries the screen, so there is no bare-metal spot to mask before powder coat."
    }
  ],
